# Database safety

The development database has been lost before. Do not take any action that can drop, reset, or overwrite a database or its credentials.

- Never run `neonctl`, `psql`, or any command that creates, deletes, or resets Neon branches or projects.
- Never run `DROP`, `TRUNCATE`, or `DELETE` without a `WHERE` clause against a real database.
- Never read, print, edit, or overwrite `.env` files (`.env`, `.env.local`, `.env.*`).
- The only allowed database commands are `npm run db:migrate` (development) and `npm run test`.
- Live checks only on small throwaway trees that you create and delete yourself.
- Stop all dev servers when finished.

```bash
# ❌ BAD
neonctl branches delete dev
psql "$DATABASE_URL" -c "DROP TABLE persons"
# ✅ GOOD
npm test
npm run db:migrate
```
